WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.790
Kids love a Disney Princess, and who can blame
them?

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.490
They're kind, they're caring, and they're
usually pretty badass, too.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.379
If you're a grown-up, however, you might notice
a whole different side to these iconic movie

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.379
characters.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:16.800
Here are some things only adults notice about
Disney princesses.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.090
It's not all that easy pinning down Beauty
and the Beast's time frame.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.490
The movie falls into that generic post-medieval
era to which so many other fairy tales belong

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.750
— you know, the kind of time where the gowns
all have hoop skirts, but where there aren't

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.870
so many knights in shining armor around.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:39.429
However, Luke Evans, who plays Gaston in 2017's
Beauty and the Beast, narrowed the era down

00:00:39.429 --> 00:00:43.250
considerably in an interview with Entertainment
Weekly, saying:

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:48.989
"When [Gaston] was about 16, he protected
the town from a pack of Portuguese marauders

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:50.390
in 1740."

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:55.460
Based on this assertion, you can safely assume
that Beauty and the Beast takes place in the

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.510
1750s, perhaps as late as 1760.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:03.850
And sure, the reign of Louis XV serves as
a good backdrop for this beloved romance...

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:07.100
until you remember what happened a couple
of decades later.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.740
Yes, it seems likely that Belle and the Beast
are going to find themselves in a spot of

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.820
bother once the French Revolution comes around
in 1789.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:19.770
Luckily, their grisly fate isn't quite set
in stone.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:25.049
In 2020, Disney launched The Queen's Council,
a new line of historical novels that intertwine

00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:28.640
their heroines' stories with actual historical
events.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.230
And sure enough, Rebel Rose, the first book
in the series, finds Belle living in 1789.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.670
She's just freed the Beast from his spell,
but the Revolution is coming to town — and

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:44.040
she soon finds herself torn between her roots
as a commoner and her future as a royal.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.899
Sounds like she'd better start teaching Lumiere
the words to "La Marseillaise."

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:54.180
Kids will be easily swept up in Pocahontas'
tale of conflict, harmony, and sentient willow

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.180
trees.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.450
But adults will likely be aware of just how
much Disney's version differs from the actual

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.450
story.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.350
So what are the biggest differences between
real life and the silver screen?

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:09.229
Well, firstly, the woman known as Pocahontas
wasn't actually called Pocahontas.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.700
She was named Amonute, and sometimes also
known as Matoaka.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:18.320
"Pocahontas" was a nickname meaning "little
wanton," which she garnered for her mischievous

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.320
nature.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.190
"Little" is the key word there, of course,
because Pocahontas certainly was little.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.690
In fact, she was roughly 11 or 12 when she
rescued John Smith.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.629
Even the veracity of that rescue is in doubt,
however, as some historians suggest Smith

00:02:32.629 --> 00:02:35.989
lifted the tale entirely from a popular ballad.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:40.799
Pocahontas was later kidnapped by an English
colonist and used as a bargaining chip during

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:42.880
the First Anglo-Powhatan War.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.870
She was eventually taken to another English
settlement, where she converted to Christianity,

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:52.739
took the name Rebecca, and accepted a marriage
proposal from a man named John Rolfe.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:57.510
Though this marriage led to a truce known
as the "Peace of Pocahontas," the woman herself

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:03.069
died in England only a handful of years after
her marriage, at the age of 21.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:07.200
Disney isn't the first to co-opt Pocahontas
for their own purposes, and they won't be

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.870
the last — but that doesn't change the awful
truth behind her real-life story.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.960
Mulan has got to be one of the most courageous
Disney Princesses of all.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.590
Despite her lack of training, her insecurities,
and the limitations placed on her because

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.050
of her gender, Mulan goes to war in her father's
place.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:29.680
Luckily, everything turns out pretty much
okay — she saves the day, wins the war,

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.400
and reunites with her father.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.430
Not every version of Mulan's tale ends so
well, however.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:38.610
If you're familiar with the ancient folk stories
that inspired Mulan, you'll know that her

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:43.519
story has carried all kinds of moral lessons
over the years, including a few that aren't

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:44.519
exactly family-friendly.

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:51.599
For example, Chu Renhuo, author of the late-17th
century Romance of Sui and Tang, depicts Mulan

00:03:51.599 --> 00:03:57.019
as a virtuous warrior — one who becomes
a sworn sister to the benighted Princess Xianniang.

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:02.090
Tragically, the respect she earns while posing
as a man pretty much vanishes when it's revealed

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.930
that she's actually a woman.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:09.040
Rather than be forced into concubinage, Mulan
cuts her own throat over her father's grave.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.870
And this is just one of many versions of Mulan's
story; one that demonstrates just how much

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:17.440
a story can change over the course of history.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.760
The Princess and the Frog is unique among
Disney movies in that it has a very specific,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.620
real-world setting: New Orleans in 1928.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:30.500
Granted, there are a few liberties taken here
and there, but by and large, Tiana lives in

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.330
the world as we know it.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:37.250
World War I took her father from her, so-called
sugar barons and cotton kings dominate the

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:42.750
Louisiana she lives in, and businessmen dismiss
her ambitions for regrettably predictable

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.750
reasons.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:48.800
"A little woman of your background would have
had her hands full trying to run a big business

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.340
like that."

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.300
Of course, Tiana ends up proving the naysayers
wrong.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.650
Best of all, even her success is rooted in
history.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:02.070
Tiana was inspired by Leah Chase, a legendary
chef known as the "Queen of Creole Cuisine."

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.910
Her restaurant, Dooky Chase, is an American
landmark, having become a gathering place

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:12.389
for the members of the Civil Rights Movement,
a dazzling art gallery, and of course, a celebrated

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:13.980
beacon of Creole cooking.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:19.310
Dooky Chase has served leaders and luminaries
ranging from Barack Obama to Ray Charles,

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:22.490
who even mentions the restaurant in "Early
Morning Blues."

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:28.430
Chase, who was delighted to serve as the inspiration
for Tiana, passed away in 2019 at the age

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.430
of 96.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:34.560
Her legacy lives on in her restaurant, her
cooking, and, of course, The Princess and

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.560
the Frog.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:37.860
What is a Disney princess?

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:41.390
Well, that's easy — it's a princess from
a Disney movie, right?

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:43.669
And sure, things can get a little fuzzy…

00:05:43.669 --> 00:05:46.740
"Okay, first, I'm not a princess.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.270
I'm the daughter of the chief."

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:49.270
"Same difference."

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.270
"No."

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:53.500
"If you wear a dress and you have an animal
sidekick, you’re a princess."

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.710
...but the definition generally holds.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.380
Then again, what about Mulan?

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.860
As a commoner, albeit one of great distinction,
Mulan isn't a princess, even by the most generous

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.640
definition of the word.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:09.639
Moreover, neither Elsa nor Anna from Frozen
are considered official Disney princesses.

00:06:09.639 --> 00:06:13.669
Even if you allow for Elsa's exclusion, given
the fact that she is a Queen, that doesn't

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:17.360
explain why Anna wasn't considered one when
the first movie came out.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.360
In reality, 'what makes a Disney princess?'
is a question with no real answer, and the

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.979
literal definition of a princess has never
really mattered much.

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:31.300
As long-time Disney fans might recall, Mulan
has been part of the line from the very beginning,

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:35.819
as was Tinker Bell — until she was removed
to lead the Disney Fairies franchise.

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:40.380
Even Anna and Elsa's position has also grown
murkier in recent years.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:45.259
Their inclusion in Ralph Breaks the Internet's
princess-centric scenes can be taken as evidence

00:06:45.259 --> 00:06:50.520
that they are now considered Disney Princesses,
yet they remain absent from the official Disney

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.520
Princess website.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.560
So what gives?

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.710
What actually makes a Disney Princess?

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.310
For now, the answer remains a mystery.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:03.740
Believe it or not, some people weren't exactly
keen on the idea of a line of Disney Princesses.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:08.819
Roy E. Disney, Walt Disney's nephew and a
longtime executive at the company, was among

00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:11.419
the most outspoken critics of the franchise.

00:07:11.419 --> 00:07:16.040
He believed that bringing the princesses together
under one brand would basically destroy the

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.840
value of their movies.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.580
This had been the prevailing wisdom for years,
too.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:25.640
Once upon a time, an Ariel doll would have
been very clearly marketed as a Little Mermaid,

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:29.470
while a Jasmine doll would have been marketed
as an Aladdin toy.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:33.789
Disney and those of like minds believed that
the movies were the core of the company, and

00:07:33.789 --> 00:07:36.259
shouldn't be messed with under any circumstance.

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:41.599
Obviously, the Disney Princess idea prevailed,
and went on to earn the company billions of

00:07:41.599 --> 00:07:42.599
dollars.

00:07:42.599 --> 00:07:45.139
But the critics managed to win a few concessions.

00:07:45.139 --> 00:07:49.669
For example, each princess is distinguished
by a signature color, meaning that Aurora's

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:54.509
infamously color-changing dress was made to
settle on pink, so as not to compete with

00:07:54.509 --> 00:07:55.509
Cinderella.

00:07:55.509 --> 00:08:00.120
Strangest of all, however, it was agreed that
the princesses should never make eye contact.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.919
Whether they appeared together on backpacks,
cereal boxes, and posters, they were to give

00:08:04.919 --> 00:08:09.580
no indication that they existed on the same
plane as the princess beside them.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:14.540
These days, however, you've got to assume
that this rule is no longer strictly observed,

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:15.770
given — well, this.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:17.389
"Do you have daddy issues?"

00:08:17.389 --> 00:08:19.130
"I don't even have a mom!"

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.130
"Neither do we!"

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:25.280
Picture this: a band of heroes from a range
of Disney movies gather together to fight

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.979
evil in one epic blockbuster movie.

00:08:27.979 --> 00:08:31.900
Sure, your mind might go to these guys, but
forget about them for a minute.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.170
What about a movie that brings together every
Disney princess?

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:40.200
Of course, an idea like that would have seemed
absurd once, but in the era of the cinematic

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:45.350
universe, all things are possible — as Ralph
Breaks the Internet proved back in 2018.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:50.390
Though the Disney Princesses take up little
of Ralph's runtime, they made a huge impact

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:52.900
on the discourse surrounding the movie.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:57.450
Multiple news items dissecting, discussing,
and celebrating the scene sprung up in the

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:02.600
movie's wake, a boatload of merchandise of
the princesses in their loungewear was released,

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:07.070
and fan speculation over a pan-princess movie
began in earnest.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.500
And these aren't just idle fan rumors, either.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:14.940
Ralph directors Phil Johnston and Rich Moore
have considered the possibility themselves.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:16.520
In an interview with The A.V.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:21.150
Club, Moore called it, quote, "an idea worth
exploring," revealing that no matter where

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:25.070
the movie played, "fans [were] off the charts"
about the princess scene.

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:29.770
Though they noted that they have no idea if
this is an idea that Disney is considering,

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:33.920
the fact that it was brought up at all shows
that there's some serious creative interest

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.190
about a Disney Princess crossover movie.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:41.630
The world of Disney Princess merchandise is
vast and ever-expanding.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:45.580
Even the luckiest kid in the world couldn't
hope to own every single Princess-branded

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:50.000
item pushed out into the marketplace — and
that's only counting the stuff explicitly

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.130
meant for kids.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:55.830
While most Disney Princess merch is indeed
for children, there's a whole range of products

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:59.760
featuring Disney Princesses that's squarely
aimed at grown-ups.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:00.900
Considering tying the knot?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:05.380
You can now put a Disney Princess engagement
ring on it, then walk down the aisle in a

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:06.860
Disney Princess wedding dress.

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:09.460
Want to keep the Disney spirit alive as you
eat?

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:14.160
You can buy a 16-piece dinnerware set inspired
by your heroine of choice.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:16.080
Looking to primp in princess style?

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:19.890
Then drop a few hundred bucks on some Disney
Princess-branded makeup.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:24.631
You can even liven up boring, grown-up tasks
like meal planning and bill payment with the

00:10:24.631 --> 00:10:26.400
official Disney Princess planner.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.780
You can't say they don't go all-out, can you?

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.940
Ideally, a trip to a Disney park should feel
effortlessly magical.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:38.312
And the passion these parks inspire in their
legions of devotees proves that, most of the

00:10:38.312 --> 00:10:41.100
time, Disney just about pulls it off.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:44.880
But when it comes to hanging out with the
princesses themselves, things start feeling

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.160
a lot less effortless.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.200
Now, meeting the princesses is certainly possible.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:53.600
They're placed all over the park, and are
usually available for photos, autographs,

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.940
and tearful confessions of childhood love.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:11:00.390
But then there are the rarer events, like
Cinderella's Royal Table, a luxurious meal

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:04.570
at Cinderella's Castle that features appearances
from the princesses themselves.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:09.940
These events are a whole lot harder to attend,
and thousands of posts, articles, and blogs

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:13.280
exist that aim to help park goers wrangle
a reservation.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:18.650
According to one intrepid mom, Cinderella's
Royal Table requires an aspiring dinner guest

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:24.640
call exactly 180 days prior to the desired
date, at precisely 7 AM.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.650
Not even that is foolproof, however, and some
gurus suggest making multiple reservations,

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.070
lest one time become untenable.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:36.760
This sort of reservation-hoarding is controversial,
to say the least, but when it comes to making

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:41.490
the magic happen for little ones, most parents
are willing to play a little dirty.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.940
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:47.580
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:51.210
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

